## Bitcoin Core `base58_encode_decode.json`

`src/base58_vectors.zig` reproduces, in full, the official plain-base58
encode/decode conformance corpus published by the Bitcoin Core project at
`src/test/data/base58_encode_decode.json` (fetched 2026-08 from `master`).
All 21 `[hex, base58]` pairs are included verbatim, transcribed by script.
This replaces what had been this module's only base58 vector — a value
independently derived by the same author who wrote `base58.zig`, using a
throwaway Python bignum script, while authoring the module (still kept
alongside, labelled as self-derived, since it separately exercises
Base58Check's version-byte-and-checksum framing that this corpus does not).

